<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" description="How Yona Tree handles information when you visit Yonatree.com, watch embedded videos, join the newsletter or send a message." href="/privacy/" updated="October 25, 2026">
  <p class="tier tier--note"><strong>Draft for review.</strong> This policy describes how the website is built. Please review it with the ministry's own advisers before launch.</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Yonatree.com does not use advertising or tracking cookies. When you <strong>join the newsletter</strong>, we collect the email address you
    provide. When you <strong>send a message</strong> through the contact form, we collect your name, email address, subject and message. We
    use this information only to send you what you asked for or to reply to you.
  </p>
  <h2>Forms</h2>
  <p>
    Form submissions are processed by our hosting provider's form service and delivered to Yona Tree. Hidden "honeypot" fields are used to
    filter spam; no tracking is attached to them.
  </p>
  <h2>Embedded videos</h2>
  <p>
    Video pages show a still image until you press <em>Play</em>. Only then does the page load YouTube's privacy-enhanced player
    (youtube-nocookie.com). After that, YouTube's own privacy policy applies to your viewing.
  </p>
  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Links to retailers (such as Amazon and Google Play), Bible Gateway, and social networks take you to services with their own privacy
    practices.
  </p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time using the link in any email, or ask us to delete information you have sent by
    writing through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
